If a bounded self-adjoint tuple $Z$ has conjugate variables, then $$\label{eq:fishervariational}
 \Phi^*(Z)=\sup_{P_1=P_1^*,\ldots,P_n=P_n^*}
 \sum_{i=1}^n\left[
  2(\tau\otimes\tau)((\partial_iP_i)(Z))
  -\tau(P_i(Z)^2)\right],$$ where the supremum is over self-adjoint noncommutative polynomials. It suffices to take $P_i=(Q_i+Q_i^*)/2$ with coefficients of $Q_i$ in $\mathbb Q+i\mathbb Q$. Consequently, along a family with continuous moments and existing conjugate variables, free Fisher information is a measurable function of the parameter.

Let $C$ be a centered bounded self-adjoint $n$-tuple, let $S$ be a standard semicircular family free from $C$, and put $Z=C+\sqrt u S$, where $u>0$. For a multi-index $\mathbf j=(j_1,\ldots,j_r)$, $r\geq1$, and a monomial $P$ in the indeterminates $x_1,\ldots,x_n$, define $$D_{\mathbf j}(P)
 =\sum_{P=P_0x_{j_1}P_1\cdots x_{j_r}P_r}
       \prod_{a=0}^r\tau(P_a(Z)).$$ The sum selects increasing positions with the prescribed indices; empty gap words $P_a$ contribute one. Extend $D_{\mathbf j}$ linearly to polynomials. There is an orthonormal family of semicircular Wick polynomials $U_{\mathbf j}(S)$, indexed by all such multi-indices, with $$\label{eq:wicktest}
 D_{\mathbf j}(P)=u^{-r/2}\tau(U_{\mathbf j}(S)^*P(Z)).$$ In particular, the conjugate variables of $Z$ exist and are $$\xi_i=u^{-1/2}E[S_i\mid W^*(Z)].$$

Let $C$ be a centered bounded self-adjoint $n$-tuple with diagonal covariance $\tau(C_iC_j)=\delta_{ij}c_i$, where $c_i\geq0$, and let $S$ be a standard semicircular family free from $C$. Put $V_u=C+\sqrt u S$ and $v_i(u)=u+c_i$ for $u>0$. For every $u>0$, $$\sum_i\frac1{v_i(u)}\leq\Phi^*(V_u)\leq\frac n u.$$ Whenever $\sum_{r\geq2}u^{-r}\|\kappa_{r+1}(C)\|_2^2<\infty$, $$\label{eq:fisherbound}
 0\leq\Phi^*(V_u)-\sum_i\frac1{v_i(u)}
 \leq\frac1{u^2}\sum_{r\geq2}u^{-r}\|\kappa_{r+1}(C)\|_2^2.$$

For the fixed tuple $X=V_h$, fix a cutoff $R>0$ with $\chi_R(X)>-\infty$. There are dimensions tending to infinity and random tuples $A^{(d)}$, uniform on increasingly accurate positive-volume microstate sets at cutoff $R$, such that, for independent standard GUE tuples, $$\label{eq:flowlower}
 \limsup_d H_d(A^{(d)}+\sqrt t G^{(d)})
 \geq\chi_R(X)+\frac12\int_0^t\Phi^*(V_{h+s})\,ds.$$ The left side is the limsup of the normalized entropies of these particular ensembles.
